    "question": {
      ":question/id": "e2244011-f203-5e23-b9b7-6125b4eee71b",
      ":question/problem": "Given that $y=4\\cdot {2}^{2x-3{x}^{3}}$, find $\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}x}$.\n\n$\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}x}=$\n{{field-1}}",
      ":question/worked-solution": "First, we express $y$ as the composite function\n\n$$\ny=4\\cdot {2}^{u},\\,u=2x-3{x}^{3}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}u}=4\\cdot {2}^{u}\\ln(2),\\,\\frac{\\mathrm{d}u}{\\mathrm{d}x}=2-9{x}^{2}.\n$$\n\nWe now apply the chain rule and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}x} & =\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\mathrm{d}u}{\\mathrm{d}x} \\\\ & =4\\cdot {2}^{u}\\ln(2)\\cdot (2-9{x}^{2}) \\\\ & =(2-9{x}^{2})\\cdot 4\\cdot {2}^{u}\\ln(2) \\\\ & =(8-36{x}^{2})\\cdot {2}^{2x-3{x}^{3}}\\ln(2).\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "6eb98a6f-a059-5b15-945c-eea698d4a8bc",
          ":answer-field/key": "field-1",
          ":answer-field/type": ":answer-field.type/blank",
          ":answer-field/choices": [
            {
              ":answer/id": "eebe02c0-50f0-5ec3-999f-7348b61e3728",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/math",
              ":answer/value": "4 \\cdot 2^{- 3 x^{3} + 2 x} \\left(2 - 9 x^{2}\\right) \\ln{\\left(2 \\right)}"
            }
          ],
          ":answer-field/correct": [
            ":answer/id",
            "eebe02c0-50f0-5ec3-999f-7348b61e3728"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
